#: 9c57afaf660e4037be40853a3ef771a3
msgid "Torch Compatibility Principles"
msgstr "Torch 兼容性原则"

#: ad1186fd5e6446f2a6df21508de10513
msgid "Status: Accepted"
msgstr ""

#: 61a74b22e3014bd08a25be07acf560f2
msgid "Last reviewed: 2026-08-12"
msgstr ""

#: 359f75e48d4641bdabe570bc2c35014e
msgid "Baseline: `582fc51d`"
msgstr ""

#: 2b1b821fe2774de69321bf11c7dc0dc8
msgid "Owner: compatibility and core maintainers"
msgstr ""

#: aab9ec2f824043edb414854cafc59980
msgid ""
"Review when: a new compatibility layer, fallback policy, or downstream "
"patch mechanism is proposed"
msgstr ""

#: 3f376d2518ca4f30b5421d723c073929
msgid ""
"Torch compatibility is a means to run useful workloads with Jittor "
"semantics and Jittor devices. It is not permission to copy every Torch "
"namespace into one module or to report success while computation has "
"escaped to another runtime."
msgstr ""

#: b0591da45e884c939913dbb738504470
msgid "Goals"
msgstr ""

#: 1d71926c3fcf44aebde97814489c27e1
msgid "Compatibility work must satisfy five gates:"
msgstr ""

#: b055d45f04e24eb9b2d708082803c296
msgid ""
"**G1, semantic correctness:** outputs, dtypes, shapes, errors, gradients,"
" and state transitions match the documented contract for supported "
"inputs."
msgstr ""

#: 6c81ee5a55064c5cb95acbd2c2850620
msgid ""
"**G2, device execution:** advertised CUDA, ROCm, or NPU operations "
"execute on that backend; host conversion is not an accelerator "
"implementation."
msgstr ""

#: 67e329f68ef64ae18cac8ab17314c57b
msgid ""
"**G3, composition:** the API works through the public import path used by"
" real applications, including registration and serialization boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: 75616864995b4faa85e5d350f582a648
msgid ""
"**G4, maintainability:** capability has one owner, failures are "
"observable, and version-specific behavior is isolated."
msgstr ""

#: d8d59f514730473a97f9c59494e8f50e
msgid ""
"**G5, evidence:** regression tests and, where performance is material, "
"reproducible benchmarks support the claim."
msgstr ""

#: f3fc3c7c9ddd4efaac9664fcce8cb69a
msgid "Ownership decision"
msgstr ""

#: ad360f31eab644e696647e0369221fe3
msgid "Use the lowest reusable layer that correctly owns the behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: 376460f426c345e3bccaacb6fb6d92d5
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: 5ec0068312ea4e39baca9f612a501d4d
msgid "Owner"
msgstr ""

#: fca0df21be7f4967b53aafe48a3c8c70
msgid "Tensor semantics, gradients, dtype/device rules"
msgstr ""

#: d5ab315162214726823b7fa874e8b15a
msgid "Jittor core or native domain"
msgstr ""

#: a507bd9a6627457b8602c508428d12a4
msgid "General neural-network operation"
msgstr ""

#: e1685c341b6e48fda3637af1acbab683
msgid "`jittor.nn`"
msgstr ""

#: f3d8f72c798947909f398fac4c612a17
msgid "Torch spelling or argument adaptation"
msgstr ""

#: e16639fd26ff4393bd5bbae4f979d6bc
msgid "`jittor.compat.torch`"
msgstr ""

#: d46a3ca49686435fa3d5715d39ed4492
msgid "Reusable import/build/patch mechanism"
msgstr ""

#: 8fe4491f268e4413913f084281a7eea8
msgid "`jittor.compat`"
msgstr ""

#: 0dfb26bf44ef47c1a789a98f0f9f604f
msgid "Torch shim runtime/deploy and top-level `torch` surface"
msgstr ""

#: 8f36a231ef714bc49164dd76087eb1d3
msgid "`jittor.compat.shim`"
msgstr ""

#: 2ee463ae21064348aebddda6ceea4126
msgid "Triton API bridge"
msgstr ""

#: bf55787003db4502a4008ce5ee772a8c
msgid "`jittor.compat.triton`"
msgstr ""

#: 1c0cacdff6fa4b4cbef1ebf45af18a10
msgid "One project's model/version glue"
msgstr ""

#: 170ebca39af9424882e895c2797a11ea
msgid "an optional integration package"
msgstr ""

#: b0c4c12aa0b14c53be11cceecd586047
msgid ""
"If several downstream projects need the same operation, promote the "
"operation to the native domain. If they only need the same patching "
"mechanism, promote the mechanism while leaving each patch outside core."
msgstr ""

#: 17e3156e8aa6425a9ab57e273c3781ac
msgid "Correctness rules"
msgstr ""

#: 270ed4d1a8684b1bba96de91a42015fa
msgid ""
"Compare against an independent oracle or written contract, not another "
"alias of the implementation under test."
msgstr ""

#: dde8e6acb89e48a0b48cda536886f628
msgid ""
"Cover positional and keyword forms, dtype promotion, broadcasting, empty "
"and non-contiguous inputs, device selection, gradients, and stateful "
"behavior when relevant."
msgstr ""

#: c30479596064478baab85831fd26dc67
msgid ""
"An unsupported contract raises a focused error. Returning a plausible but"
" wrong value is never an acceptable fallback."
msgstr ""

#: f28aecb16d254a2e846efcec4c1349e7
msgid ""
"A compatibility wrapper must not globally change unrelated native Jittor "
"semantics unless the native behavior is itself corrected and tested."
msgstr ""

#: 33a219922de242238cf90bd2d908fb66
msgid ""
"Import and installer steps are idempotent and report each failed "
"component independently."
msgstr ""

#: f956df3bd21b432284c264b8a7e2f97b
msgid "Device and fallback rules"
msgstr ""

#: 2328f2d36ea64c0cbc2374adbd11539f
msgid ""
"Host-side NumPy may be used as a test oracle or an explicitly documented "
"CPU-only implementation. It must not sit behind an API advertised as "
"CUDA, ROCm, or NPU capable. A backend fallback is acceptable only when "
"all of these hold:"
msgstr ""

#: 1927e23509b441699f19194ae0a5f639
msgid "the public contract permits the fallback;"
msgstr ""

#: 8a05404459324d1ca3319f5902a3d820
msgid "device transfer is explicit and observable;"
msgstr ""

#: 9b4626f22ec344bd9978e649009921fa
msgid "gradients and dtype behavior remain correct;"
msgstr ""

#: 9a7d593476fb4fbca1bce6bbe1047a35
msgid "the performance impact is documented;"
msgstr ""

#: 146ec929f32b4f4db0aa4a1ee57dd5b7
msgid "a test distinguishes fallback from native execution."
msgstr ""

#: 0bf4e3038adb469cafe9c5978209f116
msgid ""
"Backend availability is probed by a small real operation. Environment "
"failures and framework defects are recorded separately; neither becomes a"
" blanket skip."
msgstr ""

#: 3b75efedb1514508b1c1036eebf06427
msgid "Performance rules"
msgstr ""

#: 1b7a20f4ec68433c99fc8e378337269e
msgid ""
"Correctness is required before optimization. Performance claims use "
"warmup, synchronization, fixed shapes/dtypes, isolated caches, and an "
"exact revision. Compare equivalent execution modes and report both "
"latency and memory when the change affects either. See [performance "
"benchmarking](../performance/benchmarking.md)."
msgstr ""

#: cb0f2a8af19543b4a359ea2c38f8d2ef
msgid ""
"An optimization must retain a reliable fallback and a way to prove which "
"path executed. It may not weaken error reporting or test coverage to "
"improve a headline number."
msgstr ""

#: de83d39f811a478eba96e9bedfe9331f
msgid "Compatibility aliases"
msgstr ""

#: fba48a8262be41c28a4a73944bad1af8
msgid ""
"Aliases preserve imports; they do not preserve duplicate source trees. A "
"legacy name must resolve to the canonical module or callable object "
"whenever observable identity matters. Every new alias documents:"
msgstr ""

#: 5e0587ada8b545f691cbe7084282b1bf
msgid "the canonical path;"
msgstr ""

#: 0d31fb7279134f75b64fe6fae67af59d
msgid "the compatibility promise it serves;"
msgstr ""

#: 53683f7c8c524041b011aff9fbd11a70
msgid "tests for identity and import order;"
msgstr ""

#: 1ed6de9b32aa4b05a2cdfe3686f3e3ec
msgid "the condition under which it can be retired."
msgstr ""

#: 82cdd2f8320948808800e32ff98bde33
msgid ""
"In particular, `jittor.torch_shim` is a same-object legacy alias of the "
"canonical `jittor.compat.shim` package. The deployed top-level `torch` "
"surface delegates to that canonical runtime rather than owning a second "
"implementation."
msgstr ""

#: c461c8d5d3da40d28644c93d873d8eaf
msgid "Minimum evidence"
msgstr ""

#: 3ec7311ef82e4ae7b0f1f7e137dffb41
msgid "A compatibility change should include the smallest applicable set:"
msgstr ""

#: e4c5df677981470588e437c48484c33c
msgid "focused unit and error-contract tests;"
msgstr ""

#: 0f9ee2b38dba427282be271aa9b6634d
msgid "CPU reference comparison;"
msgstr ""

#: 4aa7fbb9f9464c4da57ae772a2c37e44
msgid "gradient and second-order gradient checks when supported;"
msgstr ""

#: 77f8df2beac74720b7977dc77a8196d5
msgid "CPU-to-accelerator parity on each advertised backend;"
msgstr ""

#: a1460112036b4b99b3b8737d707dabba
msgid "import-order, identity, and repeated-install tests;"
msgstr ""

#: d19f0e90c77d4edc9f5a0720cff266a3
msgid "a real downstream smoke test for integration-facing work;"
msgstr ""

#: 14d881529dbc41c5a6e3b7ffb50bbf4a
msgid "benchmark evidence for a claimed fast path."
msgstr ""

#: 8318ff7ae5d347389006d436a2714a49
msgid ""
"Record persistent limitations in the [known-issues "
"ledger](https://github.com/Jittor/jittor/blob/master/agent/manuals/known-"
"issues.md), with an owner and a test or reproduction that signals when "
"the limitation is gone."
msgstr ""
